1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,400
 Adding an application into ASP build system is pretty straightforward.

2
00:00:06,400 --> 00:00:13,320
 Let's have a look at the steps to add Java and Kotlin apps to the AOSP build system.

3
00:00:13,320 --> 00:00:15,960
 There are two ways to add apps.

4
00:00:15,960 --> 00:00:22,400
 One is to add the complete project with the source code into the AOSP build system.

5
00:00:22,400 --> 00:00:28,400
 Second option is to add a compiled APK file, so that means you will create the project

6
00:00:28,400 --> 00:00:34,200
 in a separate IDE, for example Android Studio, and you will build the project and make the

7
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:39,160
 APK and only move the APK into the AOSP folder.

8
00:00:39,160 --> 00:00:45,800
 So in this session, we are going to look at point 1 and see how to add a complete Android

9
00:00:45,800 --> 00:00:48,800
 project with source code into AOSP.

10
00:00:48,800 --> 00:00:55,840
 The reason why we cannot simply copy the Android project directly into AOSP is due to the fact

11
00:00:55,840 --> 00:00:58,760
 that both uses different build system.

12
00:00:58,760 --> 00:01:06,040
 As we know, the Android application uses Gradle build system, and AOSP uses the soon build

13
00:01:06,040 --> 00:01:07,040
 system.

14
00:01:07,040 --> 00:01:10,840
 These two build systems are not compatible with each other.

15
00:01:10,840 --> 00:01:15,960
 That's the reason we have to do some manual migration steps in between.

16
00:01:15,960 --> 00:01:20,840
 So these are the steps to migrate an Android project into AOSP.

17
00:01:20,840 --> 00:01:24,720
 So first step is to restructure the folders.

18
00:01:24,720 --> 00:01:31,320
 That means we need to just extract the Java or Coding source folders and the resource folders

19
00:01:31,320 --> 00:01:33,120
 from the Android project.

20
00:01:33,120 --> 00:01:37,960
 And rest of the Gradle files are not necessary for AOSP.

21
00:01:37,960 --> 00:01:45,480
 Second step, the same Android manifest dot XML can be copied into the AOSP folders.

22
00:01:45,480 --> 00:01:47,440
 It doesn't need any changes.

23
00:01:47,440 --> 00:01:51,560
 Third step is to write the soon build scripts.

24
00:01:51,560 --> 00:01:57,840
 So we need to write the star dot BP file for the new project or the module we are going

25
00:01:57,840 --> 00:01:58,840
 to add.

26
00:01:58,840 --> 00:02:04,640
 Fourth step include the new module or the project in corresponding build scripts.

27
00:02:04,640 --> 00:02:11,600
 In the next sessions, we will do a couple of practical sessions to add a Kotlin and Java

28
00:02:11,600 --> 00:02:14,000
 project into AOSP.

29
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:19,240
 So I am using the Android automotive build in this case, but the overall steps which we

30
00:02:19,240 --> 00:02:24,440
 are following in these sessions are similar for other builds as well.

31
00:02:24,440 --> 00:02:29,720
 So in case if you have a phone built, please follow the similar steps and it should go

32
00:02:29,720 --> 00:02:30,120
 fine.

